WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.550
- Well, that's why this
next part is so unbelievable

00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:04.170
and also infuriating.

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.950
Two of your books were banned

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:08.350
by a school district in Pennsylvania.

00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:09.770
Children's books.

00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:11.110
- I mean
- Two children's books.

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:13.300
But I'm like where, what year is it?

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:14.284
- Right. So
- I was like

00:00:14.284 --> 00:00:15.117
(laughing)

00:00:15.117 --> 00:00:15.950
- and you should see my house.

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:16.783
So, I'm on Twitter

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:17.780
and all of a sudden someone tells me

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:20.070
they're like "Brad they
banned 'I am Rosa Parks'

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:21.620
and 'I am Martin Luther King Jr'."

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:23.386
I'm like, you know, I
mean, look at these, you,

00:00:23.386 --> 00:00:25.750
this is clearly trying to like,

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:26.890
do some harm here, right.

00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:29.070
- Clearly you're trying
to just destroy villages.

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:29.903
Yeah.

00:00:29.903 --> 00:00:30.890
- My wife, my wife was so pissed.

00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:32.260
My wife is like, I'm gonna kill 'em.

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:33.785
And I'm like, yeah, but I was heartbroken.

00:00:33.785 --> 00:00:35.190
Right. She's murderer.

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:36.310
- Right? Yeah.

00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:37.761
- Yeah. You know our house
now it really is true.

00:00:37.761 --> 00:00:38.910
- That's a good yin and yang
you have going on there.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:39.743
- But I was

00:00:39.743 --> 00:00:40.730
But the truth was I was heartbroken

00:00:40.730 --> 00:00:42.180
cuz like there are all these kids

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:43.730
that don't get that story now.

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:44.563
- Yeah.

00:00:44.563 --> 00:00:46.800
- And when you look at that,
I'm like, that's just crazy.

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:50.110
Cuz I don't care where, I know
race is a hard subject, but

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:52.220
- But when you shield them
from it, nothing progresses.

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:53.053
- God bless. Right.
- Yeah.

00:00:53.053 --> 00:00:54.500
- I mean the, I tell my kids all the time

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:55.390
I know it may be hard.

00:00:55.390 --> 00:00:56.330
You don't shy away from it.

00:00:56.330 --> 00:00:58.010
The only way is you gotta go through

00:00:58.010 --> 00:01:00.060
and we do our kids a huge disservice

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:01.540
if we don't discuss these issues.

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:02.430
- And we do ourselves

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:04.440
because the next generation
you're not helping them, yeah.

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:05.273
- That that's it.

00:01:05.273 --> 00:01:07.130
And, and these books are
literally designed to

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:07.990
give your kids these lessons.

00:01:07.990 --> 00:01:10.040
I have a, you know, in
the back of every book

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:11.550
there's a real photograph of the person.

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:13.010
So you see this cartoon story.

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:16.079
And, and my friend told me
this story, so he's white,

00:01:16.079 --> 00:01:17.980
his daughter's black, adopted.

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:19.997
And he says, he gets to the last page of,

00:01:19.997 --> 00:01:21.350
"I am Rosa Parks"

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:24.600
and he opens it and she sees
the real picture of Rosa Parks.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:27.410
And she says, wait a minute,
this really happened.

00:01:27.410 --> 00:01:28.770
This really happened.

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:30.010
And he said and suddenly he was having

00:01:30.010 --> 00:01:32.090
the first real conversation
about race with his daughter.

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:33.850
He's like, I'm from a mixed family.

00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:35.340
I know I should have this

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:37.820
but this is the book
that they banned Kelly.

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:39.870
And I'm like, you must be kidding me.

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:41.190
So the first thing we did of course,

00:01:41.190 --> 00:01:43.350
is we got in touch with local teachers.

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:45.401
We got in touch with, who
were incredible by the way,

00:01:45.401 --> 00:01:46.800
no one fights like a teacher.

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:48.900
- Yeah. You haven't met my mama.

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:50.650
- Oh no, trust me, we have similar moms.

00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:51.483
Right?

00:01:51.483 --> 00:01:52.316
- She's a Leo.

00:01:52.316 --> 00:01:54.670
- And, and, and what you know we did

00:01:54.670 --> 00:01:56.000
is we did what Rosa Parks taught us to do

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:58.110
and what Dr. King taught
us do, is protest.

00:01:58.110 --> 00:02:01.017
We said everyone, all the books
in this, not just our books.

00:02:01.017 --> 00:02:03.344
Books by Malala, Sonia Sotomayro,

00:02:03.344 --> 00:02:05.960
the Sesame Street book
they banned, our books.

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:07.900
We said, go buy them all and protest.

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:09.550
There were 5,000 kids in that district.

00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:12.380
And my goal, I want a every banned book,

00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:14.000
for every kid in that district.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.840
Fight back like Rosa Park taught us.

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:16.673
- Yeah.

